From: xmrblocks security audit <security@monerofund.org>
Subject: [PATCH 0004] finding 2: length-check the output-keys header before casting

show_checkcheckrawoutput() reinterpret_casts the decrypted payload to a 64-byte
account_public_address without checking that 64 bytes are actually present. The
sibling key-image handler performs exactly this check already; it was simply
omitted here.

The submitter controls both the blob and the view key that authenticates it
(xmreg::decrypt(..., prv_view_key, true) verifies against a key they chose), so
an authenticated one-byte plaintext is straightforward to produce. The 64 bytes
read past the end of the heap buffer are then rendered into the response as the
Monero address, disclosing adjacent heap memory -- which in this process
includes other users' submitted view keys.

The wording of the error message mirrors the key-image path for consistency.

Reproducer: poc/micro/f02_header_len.cpp (ASan: READ of size 64, 0 bytes after
a 21-byte region).
---
diff --git a/src/page.h b/src/page.h
index 5eed1e1..5b890e1 100644
--- a/src/page.h
+++ b/src/page.h
@@ -3888,10 +3888,21 @@ show_checkcheckrawoutput(string raw_data, string viewkey_str)
 
 
     // header is public spend and keys
     const size_t header_lenght    = 2 * sizeof(crypto::public_key);
 
+    if (decoded_raw_data.size() < header_lenght)
+    {
+        string error_msg = fmt::format(
+                "Bad data size from submitted output keys raw data.");
+
+        context["has_error"] = true;
+        context["error_msg"] = error_msg;
+
+        return mstch::render(full_page, context);
+    }
+
     // get xmr address stored in this key image file
     const account_public_address* xmr_address =
             reinterpret_cast<const account_public_address*>(
                     decoded_raw_data.data());
 
